cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "rbh-search: a reproducible search for runaway supermassive black hole wakes"
message: "If you use this software or its candidate catalogue, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tolenaar
    given-names: Boye
repository-code: "https://github.com/latteral/rbh-search"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A survey-agnostic, reproducible pipeline that searches public HST and JWST
  imaging for thin, linear, star-forming features of the kind produced by a
  runaway supermassive black hole ploughing through the circumgalactic medium.
  The pipeline is calibrated against the one confirmed example, RBH-1, and
  reports a measured selection function alongside its candidate list so that a
  null result constitutes a quantitative upper limit.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - supermassive black holes
  - gravitational wave recoil
  - Hubble Space Telescope
  - James Webb Space Telescope
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: van Dokkum
        given-names: Pieter
    title: >-
      A Candidate Runaway Supermassive Black Hole Identified by Shocks and Star
      Formation in its Wake
    journal: The Astrophysical Journal Letters
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.3847/2041-8213/acba86
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: van Dokkum
        given-names: Pieter
    title: >-
      JWST Confirmation of a Runaway Supermassive Black Hole via Its Supersonic
      Bow Shock
    journal: The Astrophysical Journal Letters
    year: 2026
